Chapter: EffectWidenArgDeny
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The wrong direction at the argument boundary. apply-narrow will only ever
 write, and says so; broad may do anything Console. Handing broad over
 would let it read where only writing was promised, so it must be refused
 with CDX2090.

 This is the half that keeps BACKLOG 1.3's fix honest. The widening at the
 argument boundary rewrites a child label to the parent the parameter
 names, and only that: Console has no dot, so no label of apply-narrow's
 covers it, nothing is rewritten, and ordinary row unification refuses the
 program exactly as before.

Section: Definitions

  broad : Text -> [Console] Nothing
  broad (t) = print-line-uni t

  apply-narrow : (Text -> [Console.Write] Nothing), Text -> [Console.Write] Nothing
  apply-narrow (f) (t) = f t

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    apply-narrow broad "refused"
  end
